-- Livestock Registry — sample farmers and livestock records (local / demo only).
--
-- The platform db-seed's load_sample_data.py is shaped for the reference
-- (farmer) registry, so LOAD_SAMPLE_DATA stays false for this variant and this
-- sample set is applied explicitly instead (see docker-compose.yml).
--
-- The Farmer Registry is the system of record for people: each livestock record
-- carries the farmer's ids and name and mirrors the Fayda FAN into
-- link_foundational_id. The Farmer rows here exist so the Farmer tab has
-- something to show and the ids line up.
--
-- Ten holdings across ten regions, each with the livestock system that region
-- actually runs: peri-urban dairy at Bishoftu, Menz sheep on the Debre Birhan
-- highlands, Abergelle goats in Tigray, pastoral camels in Somali and Afar,
-- Horro cattle in Horro Guduru, Fogera cattle on the Lake Tana floodplain.
-- Names follow Ethiopian convention: given name, father's name, grandfather's.
--
-- Farmer IDs follow the FR- + 10 digits format the livestock module validates.
-- OAN IDs follow <farmer code>-<FIRST NAME>-<###>, as _generate_oan_id builds them.
-- record_name and search_text are composed from the same fields the
-- G2PRegisterDomainService* classes use, so seeded rows match written ones.

